question:
A member of the board risk committee of a large US retail bank is reviewing an internal report on a mis-selling scandal. The report finds that:

- branch cross-selling targets were raised by 40% a year;
- branch managers received bonuses based only on the number of accounts opened;
- staff who questioned the targets were told to stop “spreading bad news”; and
- remediation costs of USD 185 million were charged to a central budget rather than to the businesses.

Which lesson about risk culture is most accurate?
